 back all production regions to v2.2.9, the most recent healthy production release that is not quarantined. Rollback status: VERIFIED in us-east, us-west, eu-west. Follow-up: confirm health and error rate recovery, decide on the v2.3.0 quarantine versus the CVE fix path, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-04"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 18191, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013sENBvF5AmsVzTGpTWKRLu", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-04", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18191, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013sENBvF5AmsVzTGpTWKRLu", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20271, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It now reports healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n- **Target version:** The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. The rollback to it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. I then rolled back to v2.2.9, the next most recent healthy release, which is not quarantined.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the v2.3.1 failure, the rollback attempt and rejection, and the v2.2.9 rollback. It also pages on-call.\n\nOpen follow-ups:\n- v2.3.0 is quarantined for a CVE, so the team needs to decide whether to take a fixed build or stay on v2.2.9.\n- v2.3.1 needs investigation before it is redeployed. Its unhealthy status is recorded in the deployment history.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking"