. Actions taken: attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the last healthy production release, but it was rejected as quarantined (CVE-2026-4417). Rolled back all production regions to v2.2.9, the most recent healthy production release that is not quarantined. Rollback status: VERIFIED in us-east, us-west, eu-west. Follow-up: confirm health and error rate recovery, decide on the v2.3.0 quarantine versus the CVE fix path, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-04"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It now reports healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n- **Target version:** The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. The rollback to it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. I then rolled back to v2.2.9, the next most recent healthy release, which is not quarantined.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the v2.3.1 failure, the rollback attempt and rejection, and the v2.2.9 rollback. It also pages on-call.\n\nOpen follow-ups:\n- v2.3.0 is quarantined for a CVE, so the team needs to decide whether to take a fixed build or stay on v2.2.9.\n- v2.3.1 needs investigation before it is redeployed. Its unhealthy status is recorded in the deployment history.", "type": "text"}]}]}